#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124142 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f232aed9-1584-5e57-a881-226a6876384a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/id #uuid "001af492-25b1-5f75-b030-668708eee118" :question/math-academy-id "e-15602" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n$x = 2 + 2t; y = 5t; z = 1 - t$\nWhat would be the vector equation of the line?" :question/worked-solution "These parametric equations are equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 + 2t \\\\ 5t \\\\ 1 - t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}2t \\\\ 5t \\\\ -t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\nr &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124143 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b3699391-68e8-5c59-8ca2-83fded9f22de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Parallel To a Straight Line Given Parametrically"}] :question/id #uuid "7a6038c2-3f7b-5dfa-a9e2-256b246fcc20" :question/math-academy-id "e-15603" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n$x = 5 - t; y = 3; z = 1$\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}5 - t \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}-t \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\nr &= \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n\nThis implies that the line passes through the point $(5,3,1)$ and is parallel to the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124144 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Line"}] :question/id #uuid "173b99e8-d00c-57c8-995e-ba198361480e" :question/math-academy-id "e-15604" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line shown in the figure below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1920/Source/Images/fc5afc43c642374b8c9fc33cd5cbe982.png)" :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(3,3,-5)$ and $Q(1,0,-1)$. Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= PQ^(→) \\\\\n&= OQ^(→) - OP^(→) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr &= p + tv \\\\\nr &= \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}-2t \\\\ -3t \\\\ 4t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}3 - 2t \\\\ 3 - 3t \\\\ -5 + 4t\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$. And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{x = 3 - 2t; y = 3 - 3t; z =-5 + 4t\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124145 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d275a218-aa12-54bd-a4ff-4be892226f4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Segment"}] :question/id #uuid "a9c13555-9d30-5dfc-be5a-13f0597c2ada" :question/math-academy-id "e-15605" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overline{PQ}$, where $P(1,-5,3)$ and $Q(0, 4, -4)$." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= PQ^(→) \\\\\n&= OQ^(→) - OP^(→) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr &= p + tv \\\\\nr &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} + t\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}-t \\\\ 9t \\\\ -7t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 - t \\\\ -5 + 9t \\\\ 3 - 7t\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t \\in [0,1]$. Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q$.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overline{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{x = 1 - t; y =-5 + 9t; z = 3 - 7t\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124755 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f1f218c-88f5-5fee-bb7e-cb06249f22b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x =-6 + 5t; y =-2 - 10t; z = 1 + 2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121550} {:answer/id #uuid "be4a43b2-e1e0-5782-9043-37cf5c79ea03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x = 5 - 6t; y =-10 - 2t; z = 2 + t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121551} {:answer/id #uuid "ef1b20bb-a77b-5407-bb4e-cfbe7f204456" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x = 5t; y =-10t; z = 2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121552} {:answer/id #uuid "4683094c-5eea-540d-8826-b4b016fbf0cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121553} {:answer/id #uuid "54b9c337-0c26-5982-9419-ff143c16e066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x =-6t; y =-2t; z = t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be4a43b2-e1e0-5782-9043-37cf5c79ea03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x = 5 - 6t; y =-10 - 2t; z = 2 + t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121551} :answer-field/id #uuid "373fa3c8-309f-5e78-9ba8-49258baf8137" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121549}] :question/id #uuid "8d475564-a068-5f4f-ac3d-e39d879d093e" :question/math-academy-id "q-22295" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the straight line that passes through $P(5,-10, 2)$ and is parallel to $v = ⟨ - 6,-2, 1⟩$."}]}
